<title>UK: Banco AGF Braseg plans $50 mln Eurobond - SocGen.</title>
<headline>Banco AGF Braseg plans $50 mln Eurobond - SocGen.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco AGF Braseg plans to issue a $50 million eight-year Eurobond in mid-February, lead manager Societe Generale said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The deal will have put and call options in years three and five. It will be priced to yield between 195 and 210 basis points over three-year U.S. Treasury notes, a Societe Generale official told Reuters.</p>
<p>Banco AGF Braseg is the banking arm of AGF Brazil, which is owned by AGF International. This, in turn, is owned by French insurer Assurances Generales de France.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
